<title>FRANCE: Metaleurop H1 96/97 profit rises.</title>
<headline>Metaleurop H1 96/97 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net						 62  vs		52</p>
<p>    Operating					 89  vs		 9</p>
<p>    Exceptional		     gain	  13  vs gain	 69</p>
<p>    Financial			 expense     42  vs expense    32</p>
<p>NOTE - The company, a unit of Preussag, gave the results in a statement. It said the improvement was achieved despite losses connected with the start up of the Nordenham lead smelter. It said increases in the dollar level and zinc prices -- the half year average zinc price was seven percent above the year-earlier level -- were beneficial. Further gains in the dollar and zinc prices since the end of March &quot;offer good perspectives for the second half of the fiscal year&quot;, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;The new Nordenham lead smelter, which came close to its nominal throughput in April and May, will also contribute to better results.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
